  "scope_input": "Scope this project.\nRequest: We started research on my local machine. You are running on a VPS. We need to modify the existing \"attention feed\" to be better suited for a message bus. by default the \"attention feed\" is an in-memory list inside one ntm process (GetAttentionFeed, internal/robot/attention_feed.go:2956). It can be backed by SQLite so events survive restarts (attention_feed.go:399-402) and we need to make it so. We need to create a stop hook that is saved to the settings.local.json file in the ntm session creation process for the /.claude/ folder. The stop hook is what fires when the agent turn is complete and can serve as the \"push\" and/or \"check messages\" reminder.\nType: code\nSources: thoughts/searchable/shared/research/2026-11-06-09-56-agent-messaging-push-stop-hooks-agent-mail.md; repository /home/debian/Dev/ntm\nOutput folder: /home/debian/Dev/ntm/thoughts/searchable/shared/plans/2026-11-06-attention-feed-message-bus",
